        "v": 11,
        "title": "Advertiser reason redaction adds country exclusion codes in v2",
        "summary": "The advertiser reason redaction vocabulary versioned as advertiser_reason_redaction_2026_09_v2 now classifies country_excluded and country_unresolved eligibility reasons as show rules, surfacing them in the ADVERTISER_SAFE_REASON_CODES set without altering the generalize or hide boundaries for other reasons. These additions let the CAPI projection layer report country-based refusals as distinct, advertiser-owned facts rather than folding them into a generic temporarily_unavailable fallback. The change is confined to the operator eligibility projection table in common/src/constants/advertiser-reason-redaction.ts.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In common/src/constants/advertiser-reason-redaction.ts, ADVERTISER_REASON_REDACTION_VERSION changed from advertiser_reason_redaction_2026_09_v1 to advertiser_reason_redaction_2026_09_v2, and the ADVERTISER_OPERATOR_REASON_CODES and ADVERTISER_SAFE_REASON_CODES arrays plus the ADVERTISER_VISIBLE_REASONS map gained new country_excluded and country_unresolved entries with 'show' kind.",
